 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "f/f freezer keeps icing up bottom drawer wont shut proper, defrosted it 2wks ago already full of ice again. indesit"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "The fact that the ice has returned so quickly after a full defrost strongly suggests a fault in the automatic defrost system, such as a failed heater or thermostat. To identify the correct replacement part for your Indesit, I need to know the exact model number. This is usually found on a sticker inside the fridge compartment, often on the side wall near the salad drawer. If you can’t reach it right now because of the ice, we can leave that until later.\n[Panel: \"To check a suitable replacement — Enter your model number below. Once we have the model I can check whether a suitable replacement is available. It's usually on a sticker inside the door or around the frame, or on the back of the appliance.\"]"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "its IB55532W, read it off the rating plate. its a static freezer tho, no auto defrost, you defrost it by hand"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "Thank you for clarifying that it’s a static freezer with no auto-defrost system. Since the ice has returned so quickly, warm air getting past the door seal is the most likely cause. Please run your fingers around the rubber seal on the freezer door to check if there are any splits, gaps, or sections where it has come away from the frame."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "just looked, bottom corner of the freezer door seal is split about 5cm and the hinge side bottom bit is flattened. paper slides straight out there, grips everywhere else"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "[Heading: Likely cause: door seal]\nThat split in the rubber seal is most likely letting warm air in, which explains why the ice has built up again so quickly. You will need to replace the door seal to stop this from happening again. I could not find a confirmed match for your specific Indesit IB55532W model number online. Please contact the manufacturer's official spares service or an approved engineer to get the correct part fitted."
  }
 ],
